runsc: skip an exiting process when setting oom_score_adj

What: when runsc cannot open a process's oom_score_adj (EACCES) because the
process has begun to exit (PF_EXITING in /proc/<pid>/stat), it skips the
process, as it already skips one that has exited, instead of failing.

Why: a process gives up its mm early in its exit, and from then on its proc
files belong to the host's root, so a runsc that is not the host's root, as
under rootless Docker, cannot open them. runsc skips a process that has exited,
but one that leads a PID namespace, as the gofer and the Sentry do, counts as
running until every process in its namespace is gone. When a container's
process exits at once, runsc start sets their oom_score_adj while they exit,
and the container failed to start with "open /proc/<pid>/oom_score_adj:
permission denied".

Verified: under rootless Docker 29.9.3 (systemd cgroup driver, cgroup v2,
kernel 5.15), docker run --rm python:3.12-slim true failed that way in 1 of 5
runs with stock runsc (with --ignore-cgroups), and with --memory 64m in 5 of 5
runs with 0001 and 0002 alone, which set the stubs first and so reach the
gofer later. With this patch it started in 15 of 15 runs, and runsc's debug log
showed the gofer and the Sentry skipped as exiting. Under rootful Docker 29.1.3
(cgroup v2, kernel 7.0) it started in 5 of 5 runs.

diff --git a/runsc/container/container.go b/runsc/container/container.go
index 6773449..fcf46e0 100644
--- a/runsc/container/container.go
+++ b/runsc/container/container.go
@@ -2411,6 +2411,13 @@ func setOOMScoreAdj(pid int, scoreAdj int) error {
 				log.Warningf("Process (%d) exited while setting oom_score_adj", pid)
 				return nil
 			}
+			// A process gives up its mm early in its exit but counts as
+			// running until all its threads are gone and, if it leads a PID
+			// namespace like the gofer and the Sentry, every process in it.
+			if processExiting(pid) {
+				log.Warningf("Process (%d) is exiting while setting oom_score_adj", pid)
+				return nil
+			}
 		}
 		return err
 	}
@@ -2425,6 +2432,25 @@ func setOOMScoreAdj(pid int, scoreAdj int) error {
 	return nil
 }
 
+// processExiting returns true if the given process has begun to exit, from
+// the PF_EXITING flag in /proc/<pid>/stat.
+func processExiting(pid int) bool {
+	data, err := os.ReadFile(fmt.Sprintf("/proc/%d/stat", pid))
+	if err != nil {
+		return false
+	}
+	// The flags are the seventh field after the command name, which is in
+	// parentheses and may contain spaces.
+	stat := string(data)
+	fields := strings.Fields(stat[strings.LastIndexByte(stat, ')')+1:])
+	if len(fields) < 7 {
+		return false
+	}
+	const pfExiting = 0x4
+	flags, err := strconv.ParseUint(fields[6], 10, 64)
+	return err == nil && flags&pfExiting != 0
+}
+
 // populateStats populates event with stats estimates based on cgroups and the
 // sentry's accounting.
 func (c *Container) populateStats(event *sentryapi.EventOut) {
